    "MSI"
  ],
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_id": "Table I",
      "description": "Judged slant as a function of the gradient of texture density, recorded in degrees of tactual-kinesthetic inclination to the vertical. Means of judgments by 10 Os and medians of their standard deviations.",
      "key_stats": [],
      "n_findings_extracted_from": 4
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The visibility of the texture of the projection-screen, together with the absence of differential blur and the resulting absence of the cue of accommodation, favored a compromise between a slanted and a frontal impression.",
    "Other factors contributing to a 'frontal tendency' include the tendency of perception to conform to the slant of the hole-screen and any residual head-motion.",
    "The method of reproduction (adjusting a board) had a constant error, leading to a discrepancy between judged slant and 'physical slant equivalent to the gradient' (judged backward slants were less than forward slants), which required a baseline correction.",
    "Individual differences were notable, especially for irregular texture, with some observers reporting no slant impression for irregular texture.",
    "The possibility that observers developed 'inferences' based on cues rather than immediate impressions during the main experiment, although a substantiation experiment was conducted to address this.",
    "The 'lesser slopes' observed in the substantiation experiment were attributed to differences in the two set-ups, implying potential limitations or reduced sensitivity in the substantiation setup."
  ],
